# Code owners for the enforcement machinery (bootstrap-v2, ADR-0044).
#
# This is the human backstop behind the self-protecting gates: a change to the gate scripts, the gate
# manifest or its schema, the CI workflows, or the always-on directive cannot merge without review from
# an owner here. The mechanism (base-branch gate execution) is the first line of defense; this file is
# the second, so weakening enforcement always takes a named owner's sign-off, not just a green check.
#
# NOTE: this file only takes effect once the repo's ruleset requires review from code owners on these
# paths. Committing it is necessary but not sufficient; enabling that rule is a repo-settings change
# (see ADR-0044), tracked separately from this PR.

# The gate scripts that ARE the enforcement (parity, aggregator, provenance, and the rest).
/.claude/skills/judge-arch/scripts/   @mdenner1234
/scripts/ci/                          @mdenner1234

# The source of truth and its contract.
/gate-manifest.json                   @mdenner1234
/docs/design/bootstrap-v2/gate-manifest.schema.json   @mdenner1234

# CI workflows: how the gates run (and the base-branch protection that stops a PR neutering them).
/.github/workflows/                   @mdenner1234
/.github/CODEOWNERS                   @mdenner1234

# The always-on directive that routes every session through the skills.
/always-on/                           @mdenner1234
/CLAUDE.md                            @mdenner1234
